                    %a{:href => "#sublattice_or_tower_weak_gravity_conjecture"} Sublattice (or tower) weak gravity conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#swampland_distance_conjecture"} Swampland distance conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#emergent_string_conjecture"} Emergent string conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ads_distance_conjecture"} AdS distance conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ads_instability_conjecture"} AdS instability conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ds_conjecture"} dS conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#transplanckian_censorship_conjecture"} Trans-planckian censorship conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#asymptotic_ds_conjecture"} Asymptotic dS conjecture
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#SwamplandCobordismConjecture"} Swampland cobordism conjecture
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#general"} General
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#de_sitter_vacua"} de Sitter vacua
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#SwamplandCobordismConjectureReferences"} Swampland cobordism conjecture
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            the term
            %em swampland
            had been introduced (
            %a{:href => "#Vafa05"}> Vafa 05
            ) to publicly highlight the basic fact that many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theory"} effective quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+state"} vacua
            will not admit a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} string theory vacuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} string theory vacuum
            is a strong constraint, hence that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            predicts many more conditions to be satisfied by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+groups"} gauge groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field content
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
            than predicted by plain
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          %p
            The terminology was motivated since the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacua"} string theory vacua
            had previously come to be called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} EFTs
            not “in” this landscape to form a space “away from the landscape”, whence the colorful imagery of a swampland.
          %p More in detail, there is supposedly a map
          #eq:PointParticleLimitMap.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtext String Vacua
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi ppl
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext effective QFT Vacua
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\text{String Vacua}
                  \\overset{\;\;ppl\;\;}{\longrightarrow}
                  \\text{effective QFT Vacua}
          %p
            that takes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacua"} string theory vacua
            to their low-energy approximation by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+state"} vacua
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theories"} effective quantum field theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFTs"} 2d SCFTs
            to obtain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            (as discussed at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} 2-spectral triple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/PointParticleLimitOfStringDiagram.png", :width => "300"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "worldline+formalism#Schubert96"} Schubert 96
          %p
            Then with language of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            or more generally of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            we may begin to formalize the situation as follows:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
                of
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
                is the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"} landscape of string theory vacua
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                of
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
                is the landscape of corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theories"} eQFTs
                that admit stringy
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
                of
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
                is the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em swampland
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
                over any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theory"} EFT
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
                of the same
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theory"} effective quantum field theory
          %p
            Making this fully precise requires saying more about what the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            in
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
            actually are, and in which ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (they will be some kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
            in an ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            which may not quite be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
          %p
            For example, part of what it means to specify a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} string theory vacuum
            is to declare the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            contained in this vacuum (subject to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field+tadpole+cancellation"} RR-field tadpole cancellation
            against
            = succeed "-charges)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O-plane"} O-plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            is supposed to be (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "D-brane#ReferencesKTheoryDescription"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in some flavour of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR-theory"} KR-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            is in the corresponding flavour of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PointParticleLimitMap"} (1)
            in in the D-brane charge “sector” of the theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext String Vacua
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi ppl
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mtext effective QFT Vacua
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext D-brane RR-charge
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext in K-theory
                            %mo }
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mtext Chern character
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo {
                            %mrow
                              %mtable
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext flux forms in
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mtext ordinary cohomology
                            %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\text{String Vacua}
                  \&amp;\overset{\;\;ppl\;\;}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\text{effective QFT Vacua}
                  \\\
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{D-brane RR-charge}
                  \\\
                  \\text{in K-theory}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \&amp;\overset{\text{Chern character}}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{flux forms in}
                  \\\
                  \\text{ordinary cohomology}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  }
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            in general does have non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            (“swampland RR-fields”) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            (choices of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/UV-completion"} UV-completion
            of the effective RR-fields). In fact it fits not just in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology+hexagon"} differential cohomology hexagon
            (see there for more) of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/CohomotopySwampland.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#SS18"} SS 18
          %p
            In contrast to this example, the literature on the “swampland” phenomenon is currently dominated by informal hand-wavy arguments. Starting with
            %a{:href => "#OoguriVafa06"} Ooguri-Vafa 06
            is an attempt to guess semi-precise rules-of-thumb for recognizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} EFTs
            in the swampland, now known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %em swampland conjectures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter spacetime
            actually appears in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacua"} string theory vacua
            or not (
            %a{:href => "#DanielssonVanRiet18"}> Danielsson-van Riet 18
            ), these swampland conjecture currently revolve around bounds on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+fields"} scalar fields
            in the theory.
          %p
            An argument that much of the existing swampland literature does not even live up to the level of rigour of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/folklore"} folklore
            string theory, and in fact that it is fundamentally flawed, is made in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Banks19"} Banks 19
          %h2#SwamplandConjectures Swampland conjectures
          %p
            The following list of statements have come (around 2020-2021) to be widely discussed in a sector of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
            community which associates with the “swampland” imagery. They are now commonly referred to and known as “conjectures”, specifically “the swampland conjectures”, but the terms used tend to remain vague/undefined and may change their intended meaning with context (not the least the notion of “state in quantum gravity”, which however in most of these statements really means: classical solitonic
            = succeed "-solution" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
            = succeed "-theory" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ElectricWeakGravityConjecture"}
          %p
            But some of these statements have been interpreted in special cases as more precise statements about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+spaces"} moduli spaces
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+manifolds"} Calabi-Yau manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjectures"} conjectures
            in the sense of established sense of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
          %h3#no_global_symmetries_conjecture No global symmetries conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              A theory coupled to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              must have no global symmetries, which means that they are either broken or gauged.
          %p
            This includes global
            = succeed "-form" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %h3#completeness_hypothesis Completeness hypothesis
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
              coupled to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              must contain physical states with all possible gauge charges consistent with
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              This immediately implies that any continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
              (i.e. a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality"} duality
              groups).
          %h3#bps_completeness_hypothesis BPS completeness hypothesis
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              If a given charge can be populated by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
          %h3#weak_gravity_conjecture Weak gravity conjecture
          %h4#electric_weak_gravity_conjecture Electric weak gravity conjecture
          %p
          #ElectricWeakGravityConjecture.num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
              weakly coupled to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+coupling"} gauge coupling
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              and charge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              satisfying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ≤
                    %msqrt
                      %mn 2
                    %mi g
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi p
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \leq \sqrt{2} g q M_p,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_p
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+mass"} Planck mass
          %p The electric weak gravity conjecture can be also formulated by stating that there must exist an electrically charged state satisfying
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mi Q
                    %mi m
                  %mo ≤
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Q
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi M
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{Q}{m} \leq \frac{Q_{\mathrm{ext}}}{M_{\mathrm{ext}}}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo =
                  %mi q
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q=q g
            is the non-quantized charge,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_{\mathrm{ext}}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_{\mathrm{ext}}
            are charge and mass of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+hole"} extremal black hole
          %h4#magnetic_weak_gravity_conjecture Magnetic weak gravity conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
              weakly coupled to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+coupling"} gauge coupling
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
              must be bounded from above by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+coupling"} gauge coupling
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi g
                    %msubsup
                      %mi M
                      %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda \leq g M_p^{(d-2)/2},
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck+mass"} Planck mass
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
          %h4#convex_hull_weak_gravity_conjecture Convex hull weak gravity conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              Given a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
              weakly coupled to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec{z}_i:=\vec{q}_i/m \in\mathbb{R}^n
              be the charge to mass ratio of a charged state
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              be the set of charged states in the theory. Then, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+hull"} convex set
              of the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo ±
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\pm\vec{z}_i\}_{i\in\I}
              must contain the unit ball as measured by the kinetic matrix of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)^n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
          %p
            This condition is a stronger statement than requiring the weak gravity conjecture to be satised for each
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
          %h4#sublattice_or_tower_weak_gravity_conjecture Sublattice (or tower) weak gravity conjecture
          %p (…)
          %h3#swampland_distance_conjecture Swampland distance conjecture
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Terminology
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              of a theory coupled to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^i
              that has no
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential"} potential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in \mathcal{M}
              there always exists another point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \in \mathcal{M}
              such that their
              %span.newWikiWord
                geodesic distance
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/geodesic+distance"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(P,Q)
              is infinite. This is called
              = succeed "." do
                %em infinite field distance limit
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The decompactification limit in compactified
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              is the standard example of infinite field distance limit.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              There exists an infinite tower of states with a mass scale
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              that becomes exponentially light at any infinite field distance limit as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi c
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi P
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(Q) \sim M(P)e^{-c d(P,Q)},
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              is a positive constant.
          %h3#emergent_string_conjecture Emergent string conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p Any infinite field distance limit is either
            %ul
              %li
                %p a decompactification limit, or
              %li
                %p a limit in which a weakly coupled string becomes tensionless.
            %p
          %p
            This is a refinement of the
            %em swampland distance conjecture
            which explicits the nature of the tower of states.
          %h3#ads_distance_conjecture AdS distance conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              Any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS"} AdS
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
              has an infinite tower of states that becomes light in the flat spacetime limit
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo →
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda\rightarrow 0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∼
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi Λ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi c
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m\sim|\Lambda|^c,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              is a constant.
          %h3#ads_instability_conjecture AdS instability conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              Any
              %span.newWikiWord
                non-supersymmetric vacuum
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/non-supersymmetric+vacuum"} ?
              is at best metastable (and eventually has to decay).
          %h3#ds_conjecture dS conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              The scalar
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential"} potential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
              weakly coupled to gravity must satisfy the following bound on its derivatives:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≥
                    %mfrac
                      %mi c
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi M
                          %mi p
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\nabla V| \geq \frac{c}{M_p}V,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\sim\mathcal{O}(1)
              is positive.
          %p The dS conjecture was further refined as it follows.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p The previous bound needs to be imposed only if the condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} min
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ∇
                      %mi j
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi M
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{min}(\nabla_i\nabla_j V) \leq -\frac{c'}{M_p^2}V,
            %p
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c'\sim\mathcal{O}(1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential"} potential
              is violated.
          %p Thanks to this refinement, only proper dS minima are excluded and not general critical points.
          %h3#transplanckian_censorship_conjecture Trans-planckian censorship conjecture
          %p (…)
          %h3#asymptotic_ds_conjecture Asymptotic dS conjecture
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              The scalar
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/potential"} potential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
              weakly coupled to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
              presents a
              %em runaway behavior
              when approaching an infinite field distance point, i.e.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ∇
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi c
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\nabla V| \geq c V,
            %p
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∼
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c\sim\mathcal{O}(1)
          %p
            This is an asymptotic version of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em dS conjecture
          %h3#SwamplandCobordismConjecture Swampland cobordism conjecture
          %p
            From
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#McNamaraVafa19"} McNamara &amp; Vafa 2019
          %p
          #OriginalSwamplandCobordismConjecture.num_prop
            %h6 Conjecture
            %p
              For any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
              theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} compactified
              on a
              = succeed "-dimensional" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+group"} cobordism group
              must vanish in degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi d
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} QG
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{\mathrm{QG}}_d = 0.
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              A rigorous discussion of a possible role of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology"} cobordism cohomology
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber21a"} Sati &amp; Schreiber 21a
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#OriginalSwamplandCobordismConjecture"}
              see
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.01877.pdf#page=83"} p. 83
              there.
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The terminology “swampland”, in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
          %ul
            %li#Vafa05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
              ,
              %em The String Landscape and the Swampland
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hepth/0509212"}> arXiv:hepth/0509212
              )
          %p Review and lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eran+Palti"}> Eran Palti
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Swampland: Introduction and Review
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.06239"} arXiv:1903.06239
            %li
              %p
                Marieke van Beest, José Calderón-Infante, Delaram Mirfendereski, Irene Valenzuela,
                %em Lectures on the Swampland Program in String Compactifications
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.01111"}> arXiv:2102.01111
                )
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#OoguriVafa06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"}> Hirosi Ooguri
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On the Geometry of the String Landscape and the Swampland
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605264"} arXiv:hep-th/0605264
            %li#BrennanCartaVafa17
              %p
                T. Daniel Brennan, Federico Carta,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em The String Landscape, the Swampland, and the Missing Corner
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.00864"}> arXiv:1711.00864
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Heidenreich"}> Ben Heidenreich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Reece"} Matthew Reece
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Rudelius"} Tom Rudelius
                %em Emergence and the Swampland Conjectures
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08698"}> arXiv:1802.08698
                )
            %li
              %p
                Hee-Cheol Kim, Houri-Christina Tarazi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em
                  Four Dimensional
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=4
                  SYM and the Swampland
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.06144"}> arXiv:1912.06144
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swampland_(physics)"} Swampland_(physics)
          %p
            Beware that the landscape literature is presently dominated by non-rigorous hand-wavy
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+phenomenology"} string phenomenology
          %ul
            %li#Banks19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Banks"}> Tom Banks
                ,
                %em On the Limits of Effective Quantum Field Theory: Eternal Inflation, Landscapes, and Other Mythical Beasts
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.12817"}> arxiv:1910.12817
                )
              %p from pages 14-22:
              %blockquote
                %p
                  these considerations lead to conclusions at odds with the seemingly similar arguments of &amp;lbrack;the
                  = succeed "&rbrack;." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/swampland+conjectures"} swampland conjectures
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                  Perturbative moduli space completely distorts the true nature of the class of consistent models.
                %p
                  It’s important to realize that the entire procedure just outlined for finding (meta) stable AdS minima of a non-perturbative effective potential is purely hypothetical and has no basis in well founded string theory calculations.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots].
                %p
                  The hypothesis of the String Landscape is entirely based on low energy effective field theory ideas about finding “vacua” by minimizing an effective potential. Everything that’s been said above indicates that this idea has no validity in genuine models of quantum gravity.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                %p The most serious issue, in my opinion, is the contention that one can make the AdS radius much larger thanthe size of the compact manifold. All well established examples of large radius AdS/CFT havea compact manifold of dimension 2 or greater whose radius is comparable to that of the AdSspace. In Appendix A we’ll present an argument based on the properties of AdS black holes,that this is in fact necessary.
                %p
                  The next step in the construction of “realistic” models involves “adding an anti-brane to break supersymmetry and make the c.c. positive”. This is supposed to be a small modification of the model, calculable in low energy effective field theory, and that seems manifestly incorrect.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                %p
                  even if one believes that the construction of meta-stable dS models is reliable, there is no clear argument about what the proper observables of the model are nor that different dS constructions are part of the same model. Neither is there an interpretation of these correlators as transition amplitudes in a quantum mechanical model.
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
                %p
                  The conclusion that effective field theorists should draw from this is that unlike super-symmetric string models in flat or AdS space-time, many of which have at least perturbative definitions as mathematical models obeying the axioms of quantum mechanics, all literature on the String Landscape is speculation based on the unfounded notion that all string models with a given amount of SUSY are part of one single model and that it makes sense to define an effective action that encompasses all string models. Every single non-perturbative construction of string models contradicts this claim
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\cdots]
          %p
            Identification of the swampland charge structure with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
          %ul
            %li#SS18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Lift+of+fractional+D-brane+charge+to+equivariant+Cohomotopy+theory"} Lift of fractional D-brane charge to equivariant Cohomotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.09679"}> arXiv:1812.09679
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/src/1812.09679v1/anc"} Python code
          %h3#de_sitter_vacua de Sitter vacua
          %p
            On the question whether
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacua"} vacua
            belong to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/swampland"} swampland
            or not:
          %ul
            %li#DanielssonVanRiet18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"}> Ulf Danielsson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Van+Riet"} Thomas Van Riet
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What if string theory has no de Sitter vacua?
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1804.01120"} arXiv:1804.01120
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218271818300070"} doi:10.1142/S0218271818300070
            %li#vanRiet18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Van+Riet"}> Thomas Van Riet
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Is dS space in the Swampland
                %a{:href => "http://sp18.fuw.edu.pl/"} StringPheno18
                (
                %a{:href => "http://sp18.fuw.edu.pl/wp-content/uploads/participants-database/thomasvanriet.pdf"}> pdf slides
                )
            %li#vanRiet18a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Van+Riet"}> Thomas Van Riet
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Status of KKLT
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://scgp.stonybrook.edu/archives/24870"} Simons summer workshop 2018
                (
                %a{:href => "http://scgp.stonybrook.edu/video_portal/video.php?id=3730"}> recording
                )
            %li#ObiedOoguriSpodyneikoVafa18
              %p
                Georges Obied,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em De Sitter Space and the Swampland
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.08362"}> arXiv:1806.08362
                )
            %li#AgrawalObiedSteinhardtVafa18
              %p
                Prateek Agrawal, Georges Obied, Paul Steinhardt,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em On the Cosmological Implications of the String Swampland
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.09718"}> arXiv:1806.09718
                )
            %li#Vafa18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"}> Cumrun Vafa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cosmology and the String Swampland
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.oist.jp/indico/event/5/"} Strings 2018
                (
                %a{:href => "https://indico.oist.jp/indico/event/5/picture/96.pdf"}> pdf slides
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fU8sJRCRz24&t=1904s"} recording
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frederik+Denef"}> Frederik Denef
                , Arthur Hebecker, Timm Wrase,
                %em The dS swampland conjecture and the Higgs potential
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.06581"}> arXiv:1807.06581
                )
            %li#Danielsson18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"}> Ulf Danielsson
                ,
                %em The quantum swampland
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.04512"}> arXiv:1809.04512
                )
              %p
                (argues that the issue with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} stringy
                de Sitter
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stabilization"} moduli stabilization
                raised in
                %a{:href => "#Sethi17"} Sethi 17
                is related to the de Sitter instability seen in QFT, according to the references
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "de+Sitter+spacetime#InPerturbativeQuantumGravity"} above
            %li
              %p
                Georges Obied,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"} Hirosi Ooguri
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                %em De Sitter Space and the Swampland
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.08362"}> arXiv:1806.08362
                )
            %li
              %p
                Jakob Moritz, Ander Retolaza, Alexander Westphal,
                %em On uplifts by warped anti-D3-branes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.06618"}> arXiv:1809.06618
                )
            %li
              %p
                Iosif Bena, Emilian Dudas, Mariana Graña, Severin Lüst,
                %em Uplifting Runaways
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.06861"}> arXiv:1809.06861
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clay+Cordova"}> Clay Cordova
                , G. Bruno De Luca,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Tomasiello"} Alessandro Tomasiello
                %em Classical de Sitter Solutions of Ten-Dimensional Supergravity
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.04147"}> arXiv:1812.04147
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmology"} cosmology
            realized in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+world+models"} brane world models
            in ambient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} AdS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %ul
            %li#BDDGS18
              %p
                Souvik Banerjee,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"} Ulf Danielsson
                %em Emergent de Sitter cosmology from decaying AdS
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1807.01570"}> arXiv:1807.01570
                )
            %li
              %p
                Souvik Banerjee,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"} Ulf Danielsson
                %em de Sitter Cosmology on an expanding bubble
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.04268"}> arXiv:1907.04268
                )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+on+G%E2%82%82-manifolds"} M-theory on G₂-manifolds
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Beatriz de Carlos,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Lukas"} Andre Lukas
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Non-perturbative vacua for M-theory on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2
                    manifolds
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409255"} arxiv:hep-th/0409255
              %p
                which concludes that with taking
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effects"} non-perturbative effects
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membrane+instantons"} membrane instantons
                into account one gets 4d vacua with vanishing and negative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
                and
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti-de Sitter spacetime
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"}> de Sitter spacetime
                ). They close by speculating that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
                might yield
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Sitter+spacetime"} de Sitter spacetime
            %li
              %p
                Johan Blåbäck,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulf+Danielsson"} Ulf Danielsson
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giuseppe+Dibitetto"} Giuseppe Dibitetto
                %em Constructing stable de Sitter in M-theory from higher curvature corrections
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.04053"}> arXiv:1902.04053
                )
              %p
                which suggests that including
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+curvature+corrections"} higher curvature corrections
                makes it work
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Iosif+Bena"}> Iosif Bena
                , Alex Buchel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Severin Lüst
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Severin+L%C3%BCst"} ?
                %em Throat destabilization (for profit and for fun)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.08094"}> arxiv:1910.08094
                )
          %div
            %h3#SwamplandCobordismConjectureReferences Swampland cobordism conjecture
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a{:href => "swampland#SwamplandCobordismConjecture"} swampland cobordism conjecture
              is the hypothesis that consistency of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory+vacuum"} vacua
              in
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-theory"} F-theory
              (hence their being in the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/landscape+of+string+theory+vacua"}> landscape
              ” instead of the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/swampland"}> swampland
              ”) requires (undefined)
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} stringy
              = succeed "-analogs" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+groups"} cobordism groups
              to vanish:
            %ul
              %li#McNamaraVafa19
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+McNamara"}> Jacob McNamara
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                  %em Cobordism Classes and the Swampland
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.10355"}> arXiv:1909.10355
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/1755441"} spire:1755441
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miguel+Montero"}> Miguel Montero
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Cobordism Conjecture, Anomalies, and the String Lamppost Principle
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.11729"} arXiv:2008.11729
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Dierigl"}> Markus Dierigl
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Heckman"} Jonathan Heckman
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the Swampland Cobordism Conjecture and Non-Abelian Duality Groups
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.00013"} arXiv:2012.00013
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirosi+Ooguri"}> Hirosi Ooguri
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"} Tadashi Takayanagi
                  %em Cobordism Conjecture in AdS
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.13953"}> arXiv:2006.13953
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  David Andriot,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nils+Carqueville"} Nils Carqueville
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niccol%C3%B2+Cribiori"} Niccolò Cribiori
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Looking for structure in the cobordism conjecture
                  %strong 13
                  (2022) 071 [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.00021"}> arXiv:2204.00021
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.21468/SciPostPhys.13.3.071"} doi:10.21468/SciPostPhys.13.3.071
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                  , Christian Kneissl, Chuying Wang,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Dynamical Cobordism Conjecture: Solutions for End-of-the-World Branes
                  %strong 2023
                  (2023) 123 [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.03423"}> arXiv:2303.03423
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP05(2023)123"} doi:10.1007/JHEP05(2023)123
            %p
              Relation to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge+quantization+in+K-theory"} D-brane charge quantization in K-theory
            %ul
              %li#BlumenhagenCribiori22
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niccol%C3%B2+Cribiori"} Niccolò Cribiori
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Open-Closed Correspondence of K-theory and Cobordism
                  %strong 2022
                  37 (2022) [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.07678"}> arXiv:2112.07678
                  ,
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP08(2022)037"} doi:10.1007/JHEP08(2022)037
              %li#BCKM23
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niccol%C3%B2+Cribiori"} Niccolò Cribiori
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Dimensional Reduction of Cobordism and K-theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => " https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP03(2023)181"} doi:10.1007/JHEP03(2023)181
                  = succeed "]" do
                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.01656"} arXiv:2208.01656
            %p Review:
            %ul
              %li#Blumenhagen23
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ralph+Blumenhagen"}> Ralph Blumenhagen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Nullifying Cobordism in Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://nyuad.nyu.edu/en/events/2023/march/quantum-field-theories-and-cobordisms.html"} QFT and Cobordism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CQTS"} CQTS
                (Mar 2023)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "Center+for+Quantum+and+Topological+Systems#BlumenhagenMar2023"} web
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Blumenhagen-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jLlE_jSH0lk"} YT
            %p
              A more concrete consequence of this conjecture is claimed (
              %a{:href => "#McNamaraVafa19"}> McNamara &amp; Vafa 2019
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1909.10355.pdf#page=31"} Sec. 5.2, 2nd paragr.
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "#BlumenhagenCribiori22"} Blumenhagen &amp; Cribiori 2022
              = succeed ";" do
                %a{:href => "#BCKM23"} Blumenhagen et al. 2023
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#Blumenhagen23"} Blumenhagen 2023
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "/nlab/files/Blumenhagen-at-QFTAndCobordism2023.pdf#page=45"} p. 23
              = succeed ";" do
                %em
                  Certain topological
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} brane charges are quantized
                  in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cobordism+cohomology"} Cobordism cohomology
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tadpole+cancellation"} tadpole cancellation
                of brane charges is to happen in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cobordism+cohomology"} Cobordism cohomology
              This kind of statement is also discussed, as a consequence of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.01877.pdf#page=83"} p. 83
            %ul
              %li#SatiSchreiber21a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} M/F-Theory as Mf-Theory
                %strong 35
                10 (2023) [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.01877"}> arXiv:2103.01877
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0129055X23500289"} doi:10.1142/S0129055X23500289
        .revisedby
